-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Treasure Island Dizzy
  Publisher   Code Masters, 1989
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dizzy 2 - Treasure Island Dizzy (1989)(Code Masters)(128K).z80
  MD5         db6ccbeb2f9c601476efab3cfd28b131

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Jao Paulo's colours: a red Dizzy, yellow palms with brown
              trunks, pale sand, stones and shells in their own colours, a
              yellow frame and a coloured panel. Source: Enhanced colours: Jao
              Paulo (Spec256).

  Pace        original (+0.30% measured in JNext 1.1.104; the actual player
              update, three seeds from each of three checkpoints; all player
              states matched; positive is slower than the original)

  Changes     1.0: Dean Woodyatt's Treasure Island Dizzy build moved to the
              128K release (AY music), his hooks at 28 MHz, whole alt ROM
              image, loading screen. 1.1: Enhanced colours from Jao Paulo's
              Spec256 conversion, off by default; three more cheats (Walk in
              water, Walk through walls, Room selector); Sinclair's whole 48K
              ROM as the alt ROM for NextZXOS 26.11; the caller's CPU speed
              restored and R kept as the original's; room and bubble drawing
              faster, with sound at its original clock.

  Note        Keys: Z and X walk, Space jumps; the game's controls menu has
              the rest. The 128K release with its AY music. Default: the
              original colours, with Dizzy on hardware sprites so he no longer
              takes the colours of the scenery he walks through. Enhanced
              paints Dizzy, the scenery, objects and panel in Jao Paulo's
              Spec256 colours; off by default. Fits a 1MB Next. Room selector:
              press C, then Z/X for columns, K/M for rows, Space to return.
              Known issues: in default Dizzy is light grey where the
              original's cell is bright white; room redraws keep the
              original's drawing order, so transitions can show briefly; the
              room selector can pick unused rooms; in JNext quiet play stays
              within about 0.3 percent of the original, the slowest 20-update
              stretch +1.98 percent, and Enhanced's busy scenes run 3.4 to 6.9
              percent faster. Missing: natural play to the end; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Immunity
   2  Walk in water
   3  Walk through walls
   4  Room selector (C)

  The archive's Treasure Island Dizzy .pok. Walk through walls' address 62242
  is mapped to bank 0. The alternate immunity at 29738 is left out because it
  damages the screen-row table.

